WEBVTT

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.750
<b>Farming Life in Another World</b>

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.540
Vampires really don't like mornings, do they?

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:51.920
But still, having Lu living here with me
has helped out in all sorts of ways.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:58.960
We should be all set for lights now.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:01.670
Wow, that's amazing!

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:03.790
But that's just basic magic.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:08.830
This has a really mild flavor.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:11.710
Do you prefer not to use salt
when you cook?

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:13.670
Nope. I just don't have any.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:14.630
Huh?

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:15.670
Salt.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.790
I've been looking for it for a while,
but I can't find any.

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.290
I'm at the point where I'm about to give u-

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.330
That's a pretty intense look on your face.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.750
Of course it is.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:25.540
Right here.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.460
This is mostly salt.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.830
We can dissolve some
then boil it to get salt.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.250
Did you not notice while you were digging?

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:36.170
That's a pretty intense look on your face.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:41.960
Good morning.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.960
Yeah. Good morning.

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:45.790
What are we doing today?

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:47.170
Let's see...

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.960
I was planning to check on
how the fruit trees are growing.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:50.710
Okay.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.420
I'm going to get washed up,
then I'll head over there.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.210
Look at these.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.080
Did you transplant them to the soil here?

00:02:59.080 --> 00:02:59.960
Yup.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.670
They need more time to grow
than the vegetables.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:06.170
I tried planting oranges
and peaches this time.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.500
I think I might plant chestnuts next time.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.080
Oh yeah?
I can't wait to see how they turn out.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.380
By the way...

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:19.790
The herb tea that Lu makes is pretty good,
but I want to drink green tea.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.170
If I remember correctly,
oolong tea and black tea

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.330
are all made from processing
the same leaves...

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.420
What is it this time?

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.420
Enough!

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:42.670
Please forgive me!

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:45.920
I understand that I was wrong
for attacking you first!

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.670
I've seen this situation play out before.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.380
Please rescue me!

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.380
Okay.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:56.750
Are you alright?

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.830
Yes, I think so.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.830
Wow, that's amazing!

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:15.170
It's nice to be able to use magic, huh?

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:16.830
Lu?

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:20.710
So this is where you were hiding, Lulucy!

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:25.170
Stop resisting and come in quietly!

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.630
Hey, hey, hey!

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:33.750
Jeez... I can't believe you hid
in this forest of all places.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.380
Well, a lot of stuff happened.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.750
That was an awful experience
I just went through.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.670
I know. They did that to me, too.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.130
You too?

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:45.670
Yeah. They're pretty ruthless.

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:48.630
Magic doesn't really affect them much,
plus they dodge spells.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:51.040
Fighting them is a death sentence...

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:52.080
Yeah...

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.380
They seem to have a shared experience.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:55.670
By the way...

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:58.080
Who is this person?

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.040
I'm...

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.540
Oh, this person is, um...

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:06.460
My husband.

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.130
Your husband?!

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:10.080
You and Lulucy are a couple?!

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.630
Huh? Yeah...

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:13.460
I wasn't expecting that.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:15.580
Um, I'm Hiraku.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.540
Her husband...

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.790
That's the first time she's called me that.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.290
Allow me to introduce myself properly.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:24.920
I'm Tia.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:27.330
As you can see, I'm an angel.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:29.670
An angel? So...

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:32.580
That means you serve God, right?

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:36.630
It's nothing that important.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:39.670
They're simply a race of warriors
that have more muscles than brains.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.580
How rude!

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:44.830
There was a brief time period when
we were an object of worship, you know!

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:48.080
So why is an angel like you
chasing down Lu?

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.170
There's a bounty on her because of
all the damage she caused in town

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:52.040
when she went on a rampage.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.920
There's a bounty on your head
because of a rampage?

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.460
Well, yeah.
There was a really annoying noble

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.710
who kept forcing me to make
medicine and drugs for them.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.130
They were so incessant with their demands

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.750
that I felt the need to
teach them a little lesson...

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.380
There was nothing little about that lesson!

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:06.670
She spends all her time researching
strange medicines and concoctions,

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.630
and then as soon as something bothers her...

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:12.250
she starts blowing everything up!
That's the problem.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:14.630
Stop making it sound like this is
something I've done multiple times!

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:16.710
That was just an accident!

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:20.500
Regardless, the fact remains that you
besmirched the honor of a noble!

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:21.210
Do you have any idea how high your bounty is?

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.330
They seem to get along pretty well.
Do you have any idea how high your bounty is?<b></b>

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.630
Well, I do think I went a little too far.

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.130
I'm surprised at how willing
you are to admit that.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:33.830
So anyways, the reason I ended up here
is because I was running from Tia.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.460
After all, she is stronger than I am.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.330
But only a little.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:42.330
Lulucy, you really have changed.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:46.540
You never used to be the kind of person
who would admit any weakness.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:47.670
Yeah, well...

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.670
I felt firsthand just how weak
I really was...

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:51.670
I see.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:53.830
Fighting that many at once
should be against the rules.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:54.880
Yeah...

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:57.040
Putting that stuff aside...

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:59.000
do you want to live here, too?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.920
Huh? Live here?

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.130
Yes, here. Right?

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:04.710
Y-yeah...

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.790
I'll show you around the crop fields and stuff.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.920
I'm sure you'll love it here, too!

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.920
Let's get going, okay?

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:13.250
Sure...

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:15.920
Look!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:19.830
These are the crop fields.
We grow lots of vegetables here!

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.000
Wow...

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:24.920
And this is our orchard. We have a lot of
different kinds of fruit growing here.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.080
Whoa...

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.790
And this...

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:29.880
is Zabuton!

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:34.960
Yeah. That's about what I expected.

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:37.210
Maybe she doesn't like spiders.

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:38.670
Hey!

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.710
We're about to harvest some crops.

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:43.330
Come with us.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.040
It's a lot of fun!

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.960
Okay...

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.580
Did you plant this all yourself, Hiraku?

00:07:51.580 --> 00:07:52.580
Yup.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.750
I helped a little, too.

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.420
I was just thinking we needed
another set of hands.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:58.580
You're really saving us here.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:02.380
Huh? You mean I'm going to
do farm work, too?

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:03.880
Of course.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:04.830
Come on!

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.750
Why does an angel like me have to
get her hands dirty with garden work?

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:10.500
Okay then, let's get started
with the cabbage.

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:19.500
Give it a try just like that.

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.460
O-okay...

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:30.330
These are pretty heavy, huh?

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:31.880
Want to give it a taste?

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:35.920
Here.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:40.290
Well, all I did was tear up some cabbage leaves
I washed and sprinkle salt on them...

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.130
It's delicious. Really!

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.250
Glad to hear it.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:53.000
Fresh vegetables really do
taste great, don't they?

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:57.330
Yeah. And the ones you grow yourself
taste even better.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:59.000
I think you're right.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:05.420
I think that's enough for today.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:07.630
Yeah, that's plenty.

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:09.380
I'm exhausted.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:13.210
It's nice to have so much
but harvesting them all is hard work.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:17.880
I wish I could do that...

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:22.630
It's delicious!

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:26.540
This vegetable you call a strawberry
is so sweet and tart.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:27.540
It sure is.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:31.460
This farming work is a lot more
fulfilling than I expected it to be.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.040
You had fun today, right?

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:34.170
Yes.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.210
Well then, that settles it!

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.080
You're going to live here with us, right?

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:39.960
Um...

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:41.580
Right? Come on, please!

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.830
My body won't be able to
handle everything if I'm alone.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:46.130
Excuse me?

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.380
What do you mean by that?

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:11.130
Tia, this farming work
really does suit you well.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:13.000
Was that supposed to be a compliment?

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.250
Of course!

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:17.710
Very well. We'll leave it at that.

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:19.250
More importantly...

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:20.500
Hiraku.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:23.830
Can we make a lot more strawberries?

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:28.670
I really wish we could, but even if
we expanded the crop fields,

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:31.000
we wouldn't be able to keep up
with all the harvesting.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:33.710
I think we're currently operating at
about maximum capacity now.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:35.540
Hm...

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:38.380
We really could use
some more help around here.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:41.880
You can just work hard enough
to make up the difference, Tia.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:44.920
What about you?
Are you sure you haven't been slacking off?

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.790
I don't think she is.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:50.790
Besides, if we grow too much

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.630
then we might not be able to finish
eating everything that we harvest.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:57.750
Oh, it's the new puppies.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.290
Their horns are already coming in.

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:04.710
Good boy.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.830
Kuro and Yuki's children...

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:11.630
had children of their own.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:14.290
They've become quite a large family of dogs.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:19.080
Before long, the puppies are going to
go off and find partners of their own.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.540
Does that mean even more puppies?

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:26.290
Now that you mention it,
that hut isn't going to be big enough.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:31.670
And so, we decided to build
a dog area next to the orchard.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:31.670
<b>Orchard</b>

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:31.670
<b>Dog Area</b>

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:38.330
It looks kind of like a horse stable,
but I'd like to think that it turned out well.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.170
For the record, I still haven't
come up with names

00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:43.670
for the next generation
after Kuroone and his siblings.

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:45.790
I want to give them names,

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:50.420
<b>Kuro</b>

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:50.420
<b>Yuki</b>

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:50.420
<b>Kuroone  Alice</b>

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:50.420
<b>Kurotwo  Ilice</b>

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:50.420
<b>Uno  Kurothree</b>

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:50.420
<b>Kurofour  Elis</b>

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:49.540
but there are so many of them that it's hard
to come up with names for everyone.

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.960
On the other hand, Zabuton's children...

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:55.460
What is it?

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:04.040
...are riding the wind
and starting a new journey.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.380
I guess they're all leaving.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:11.170
I was planning on turning the orchard
into their new home. Oh well.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:17.460
It looks like some of them are still
staying behind with us.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.460
Hey.

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:21.750
I'm going to step out for a while, too.

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:24.630
You're going off somewhere
and leaving us too, Tia?

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:27.130
No, I won't be gone for too long.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:28.130
Now then.

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:32.630
I wonder what she's going off to do.

00:12:32.630 --> 00:12:34.880
Well, she's be back before you know it.

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:36.290
You think?

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:37.960
Farming Life...

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:39.170
in Another...

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:40.250
World

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:43.750
A few days later,

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:46.630
Tia came back just like Lu said she would.

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:49.500
And she brought a bunch of girls with her.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.130
You're elves?

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:54.040
We're high elves, but you can
call us elves if you like.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.670
What's the difference?

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.920
Please introduce yourselves, everyone.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.000
I'm Lea.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.000
I'm Leef.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.170
I'm Lecott.

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:02.170
I'm Leezay.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:03.170
I'm Leely.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:04.170
I'm Leeta.

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:05.170
I'm Lees.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:06.920
You're all Le.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:09.460
Ah, you mean our names?

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:12.670
We have similar names
because we're all related.

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:15.580
We came here after Tia suggested
that we all move here.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:18.580
Please let us all live here with you!

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:20.040
Um...

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:24.420
The truth is, they all share
a very sad backstory.

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:28.710
They all used to live in a village
far to the north.

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:31.330
But most of their people were wiped out

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.460
after they got dragged into
the war of the humans.

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:36.960
Their race was scattered, and since then
they've been wandering the land

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.420
looking for a place they could
settle down and call home.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:46.080
We've been travelling through the woods
trying to get by until now.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:50.500
Without a place to settle down,
we aren't able to repopulate our race.

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:52.630
We ask that you please help us!

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:54.080
Please help us!

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.750
You can count on them to be
excellent workers.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:58.830
I implore you to help them as well.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:00.750
I think it's a good idea, too.

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:03.710
I've heard the high elves are
a very talented race.

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:06.330
You're all still pretty young, right?

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:10.290
I'm the oldest one,
and I'm just over 400 years old.

00:14:10.290 --> 00:14:13.540
I'm the youngest, and I'm about 300.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.580
I can't tell they're 100 years apart.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.250
What do you think?

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.130
It's fine, right?

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:23.040
Well, we have a lot of different
roommates living here,

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:25.880
but if you all promise to get along
then I don't have any problem with this.

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.880
Thank you very much!

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:31.750
By the way, who are the other roommates?

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:35.130
This is Zabuton.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.750
And these...

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:40.880
are the dogs.

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:46.500
Yeah, that's about how
I expected it to go.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:49.210
The number of people living here
went up all of a sudden,

00:14:49.210 --> 00:14:50.880
so we needed to build
somewhere for them all to live.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:54.380
Lea said the seven of them
all wanted to live together,

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.420
so we decided to build them
one big house.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:15:00.040
First, we started with the ditch
and the wooden fence.

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:03.500
Then, we made them their own toilet
and garbage disposal area.

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:10.380
That was an unbreakable giant tree
that's harder than steel.

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:11.920
He cut it like it was nothing.

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:15.170
When it comes to construction,
they know more than I do.

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:17.170
And they're all really handy, too.

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:19.920
I even got to learn a lot about
how to process lumber

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.750
and fit the logs together from them.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:24.830
I just followed their orders.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:26.830
I focused on digging holes,

00:15:27.130 --> 00:15:28.750
and leveling the ground,

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:31.290
and gathering lumber for them.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.040
It took us ten days, and then...

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:35.710
It's finished.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:36.670
Yeah!

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.290
That's amazing.

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.790
It's so much nicer than our little hut.

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.040
It really is.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:44.790
Jealousy...

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:46.960
Is he sulking?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.420
It looks like it.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:52.420
But now I've learned it... their technique!

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:57.830
It might be a good idea to try rebuilding
the little hut we've been sleeping in.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:02.330
The house is shaped like a long rectangle
that stretches from east to west.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:04.250
Just past the entrance way,
there's the large living room

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:06.330
that doubles as a dining room.

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:10.290
It's a place to work on things together,
or so they can all eat together.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:15.170
Sitting on both the left and right sides of
the living room are storage rooms.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.790
<b>Living Room</b>

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:13.790
<b>Storage</b>

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:13.790
<b>Storage</b>

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.670
The living room is an open design
that covers the first and second floors.

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:19.630
The lighting is done with magic.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:23.380
And the second floor rooms sit
on top of the storage rooms.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:26.380
The second floor is where
their individual rooms are.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:34.250
I hope that this can become a home
where they feel safe and at peace.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:44.500
It looks like they've all
gotten used to life here.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.630
Yeah.

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:48.080
The vegetable harvesting is going great.

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.040
Yup.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.960
They're eating raw garlic they just picked.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:54.420
That's pretty wild.

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:56.500
Huh?

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.250
You use fire and you eat meat, too?

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:01.040
Yeah, of course.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:02.710
When I think of elves...

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:06.210
I think of a race that lives in the woods
and is one with nature,

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:08.040
and hates fire and stuff.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.790
Where'd you get that silly idea?

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:12.380
Am I wrong?

00:17:12.790 --> 00:17:16.040
How is anyone supposed to live
without using fire?

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:18.250
Like I said, you're one with nature...

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:19.460
Can you be more specific?

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:21.290
Huh? Well...

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:22.830
You wake up with the sunrise,

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:24.790
and go to sleep when it sets.

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:26.670
You eat fruit from the trees.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.460
And you love the forest trees.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:31.040
And you refuse to wear
anything made of metal...

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:32.580
Excuse me, Hiraku.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:33.540
Hm?

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:35.920
Please stop underestimating
how harsh nature can be.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:39.540
If you tried living like that in the forest,
you'd die right away.

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:41.170
I-I see...

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:42.330
Good.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.580
They really are hardcore survivalists.

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:48.040
By the way, as thanks for
letting us all live here,

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:51.330
we were planning on doing some mining
and blacksmithing work for you.

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:53.130
Huh? You guys can do that?

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.080
We can.

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:57.380
I'd like to start by building
a furnace that can melt iron.

00:17:58.250 --> 00:18:00.790
I always imagined that dwarves handled
all blacksmithing related work.

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:02.670
I guess that's different in this world.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:08.080
Following Lea's instructions, they quickly
put together a smithing work station.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:10.920
They put charcoal and
iron sand taken from the river

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:13.830
<b>Charcoal</b>

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:13.830
<b>Iron Sand</b>

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:13.250
into the earthen furnace and heat it up.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:15.500
Then they hammer the melted iron
to process it.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:19.830
This is great!

00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:21.420
Our civilization is advancing!

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:23.000
Thank you very much.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.630
You can really do everything, can't you?

00:18:25.630 --> 00:18:27.080
Well, that tends to happen

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:30.580
when you spend the better part of
200 years wandering without a home.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.880
I see.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:34.460
The only things we couldn't do...

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:38.130
was settle down for good and reproduce!

00:18:38.330 --> 00:18:40.540
Well, we already took care of one of those!

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.920
I thought it would be for the best

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:45.080
if I didn't say anything about
the second thing she mentioned.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:53.330
I'm really happy you guys
all came to live here.

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:54.380
Me too.

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:57.420
I'm happy to hear that you feel that way.

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:00.630
Let's stop here for today.

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:01.750
Excuse me.

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:05.920
I believe I saw a wheat field out over there.

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:07.960
Yeah, we have one,

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:11.460
but we already processed all the wheat
we harvested into flour so we could store it.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:16.420
If it's alright with you,
I'd like to bake some bread.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:19.210
Bread? Please go ahead!

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.170
What's that?

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:25.130
If you use this stuff, it makes the bread
rise up when it bakes.

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:49.290
That freshly baked bread tasted amazing.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:55.540
This is delicious!

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:56.880
It really is.

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:00.000
We're all very happy to hear that you like it.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:05.920
That jar must have had a natural yeast
to make the bread rise inside of it.

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:10.500
Now that we can bake bread,
I'd like to expand the wheat fields...

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:15.210
I know it's a little late to be asking this,

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:17.960
but does this land we're on
belong to anyone?

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:19.750
You mean like this forest?

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:20.580
Yes.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:25.330
I don't think anyone owns this
particular plot of land or anything,

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:28.080
but I guess technically it's under
the control of the demon lord.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.500
The demon lord?!

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:31.670
What the heck? That's scary.

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:33.580
Is there a problem?

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:36.330
Um... do you think the demon lord
is going to have a problem

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:39.880
with me building all these
crop fields and stuff here?

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:42.250
Is that what you're worried about?

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:46.000
Did you receive any kind of support
when you started building all this?

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:47.420
No. Not at all.

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:49.670
Then there's nothing to worry about.

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:54.580
If you built this on your own,
then the land belongs to you.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:56.630
I guess that's how it works.

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:58.460
Yeah, that's how it works!

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.330
<b>Orchard</b>

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.330
<b>Dog Area</b>

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.330
<b>Elf House</b>

00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:09.330
Hiraku is really full of surprises.

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:12.420
He surprised me a lot at first, too.

00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:16.670
Not only did he tame all those inferno wolves,

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:19.670
but he tamed a demon spider, too.

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:21.880
He's definitely special.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:24.130
And these crops...

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:27.920
Is the soil here really good enough
to grow things like this?

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:30.540
Who knows? I never asked him.

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:34.000
I'm sure he has a very green thumb.

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:39.250
That said, it's surprising how lacking he is
in knowledge about the world around him.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.330
Ah! I know what you mean.

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:47.500
He was saying that he thought elves were
a race that didn't use fire or eat meat.

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:49.170
Are you serious?

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:52.790
He didn't seem to know
what angels are, either.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:55.710
That goes a few steps beyond
just lacking some knowledge.

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.420
Yeah, you're right.

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:08.210
Oh yeah, I haven't progressed on
building the waterway in a while now.

00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:11.420
Maybe I'll ask Lea and the elves
to help me out.

00:22:11.920 --> 00:22:14.170
There's lots of work to do tomorrow.

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:47.210
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:47.210 --> 00:23:50.960
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:23:47.210 --> 00:23:50.960
<b>Waterways Make Life Feel Complete</b>

00:23:47.210 --> 00:23:50.960
<b>Next time</b>
